# Two exclusions, both deliberate. Nothing else is excluded, also on purpose:
#
# - tests/<name>/ holds field notes from adopting a project: internal, short-lived, and
#   never committed, by Costin's ruling (d-tests-folders-never-committed). Ignored here so
#   that is a check rather than a thing to remember. `git add -f` still bypasses it.
#   Anything worth keeping from one is harvested into docs/CONCERNS.yaml instead.
# - Python bytecode from scripts/.
#
# - spec/PROJECT-STANDARD.md and spec/SESSION-PROTOCOL.md are GENERATED but MUST be tracked.
#   They are the readable form of the spec, and the drift gate compares the committed file
#   against a fresh render — an untracked generated file could never drift, which would
#   silently disable the check.
# - docs/claude-memory.md is generated by the memory-mirror hook and MUST be tracked. It
#   exists precisely so agent memory is auditable from the repo; ignoring it would restore
#   the problem it was created to solve.
/tests/*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
